00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.110
And we're going to
interview some top creators

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.080
to hear some of their VidCon experiences.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.003
Let's do it. Let's go. Let's go.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:12.440
- Hey guys, I'm Manny MUA.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:13.460
- Hi, my name is Hannah Hart.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.560
- Hey, I'm Colleen Ballinger.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.000
- Hey everyone, my name is Patrick Starrr.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:16.930
- It's Alicia Marie.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.350
- I'm Rosanna Pansino.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.830
- Hi, my name is Remi Cruz.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.460
- The first time I went to VidCon,

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.890
it was at the bottom of a hotel.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.880
This was maybe like
the second VidCon ever.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.390
- I think my first one was bouncing from

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:29.310
food truck to food truck
finding ice cream, hotdogs.

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:30.890
- I just remember being really nervous,

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:33.140
being shocked that anyone knew who I was.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:36.060
- People crowding you, swarming
you, taking photos with you.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.920
I love it honestly, I
think it's freakin' great.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.400
And I'm like bitch yes, I'm like, yeah.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.700
- For me, I first started
coming as a community creator

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.610
and I remembered
specifically this one time

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.690
I was standing outside
and I saw Rebecca Black

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.210
and these other people were being like

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:48.960
ushered to the hotel across the street

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.270
and everybody was like mobbing them.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.623
I was like, one day, that's gonna be me.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.980
- I decided to do a scavenger hunt

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:56.450
with my fans through Snapchat.

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:58.360
So, I was like, okay go to this location

00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.420
and you'll get a free beach ball.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:02.330
Go to this location and
the final location was me.

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:03.363
They got to meet me.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.530
And I didn't understand how
many fans I had at VidCon.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:11.130
So, it caused like stampedes
and security got so mad at me.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.180
I had to make a formal apology to VidCon,

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.230
I felt so bad.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:18.823
- First year, I was not in any
way, shape, or form invited,

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.510
so I just kinda came, it was
actually really crazy for me.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:22.950
I needed to get security
and VidCon was like,

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.010
What are you doing here?
Why are you doing this?

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:26.340
It was such a intense moment, I was like,

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.720
I don't know, I just wanted
to come and be part of it.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.750
- Look, I don't remember what
happened the night before.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.770
What I do remember, is that I woke up

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:36.243
and my pants were covered in
ranch and in the bath tub.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.673
I wasn't wearing them. Ranch pants.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:42.150
- I'm at the top of the
escalators and I hear

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.710
mad screaming and running, and
I was so scared for my life.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:47.020
I turn around and I see

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.703
literally hundreds of people swarming.

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.560
It was Jack or Finn, one of
the twins, Jack and Finn.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:53.810
That was my introduction to VidCon.

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:56.450
I was like, "Okay, I get what it is now."

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:59.150
- One of the most special
memories that I've had at VidCon

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:01.643
actually happened this morning.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:03.300
I got to team up with Make a Wish,

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.700
and make a wish come true.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.300
I met a young girl from Texas named Maddie

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.620
and we decorated cakes
together all morning.

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:11.300
We took pictures, we had a blast.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.700
My heart is so happy right now

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.090
that I'm about to get emotional.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:16.710
But this is a memory that
will last with me forever

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:19.373
and I hope she had a great
time as well 'cause I did.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.300
- I think connecting with a community,

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.960
being actively social,
make a friend online,

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.550
make a friend in person, that
way you don't feel alone.

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:28.860
I think early on when I
started, I felt so alone.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:31.660
I'm like, "I don't know what
to do. I'm a man in makeup."

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:33.440
And then I found other men in makeup.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:35.703
Once you find your
niche or your community,

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:37.810
it'll make you feel a lot
more comfortable and grown.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:39.810
- Consistency is key,
don't get discouraged

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:41.570
if you don't get views right away.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.780
Yyou have to just keep
trekking on and keep doing it,

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:45.470
and stay consistent with your content.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:48.100
- My advice to future creators
is honestly just to start.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.440
I feel like a lot of
people get this weird thing

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:51.840
in their mind like, "I
don't have enough equipment,

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:53.090
or I don't have the best lighting.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.560
I don't have the best camera,
or anything like that."

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:55.393
It's not about that,

00:02:55.393 --> 00:02:57.220
it's literally just putting
your best foot forward.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:59.390
- I feel like the biggest
thing is just to be yourself.

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:02.060
It took me years to really get
comfortable with the camera.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.713
Before, I tried to be so perfect,

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:05.670
and no one wants to see
someone who's just perfect.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:08.913
- Find your voice, have
fun, be consistent,

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:11.880
and don't put too much
pressure on yourself.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:13.250
- People can see when you're doing YouTube

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.740
for the right reasons, so make content

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:16.220
that you would watch yourself.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:18.880
- Create content that
you are passionate about.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.540
If you love singing, sing.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:23.490
If you love comedy, you serve that comedy.

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:25.890
Whatever you love, make content about it.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.380
Because people are so
intuitive, they're so smart.

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:31.560
They know when you love what you're doing.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:32.770
- Thanks for listening to me talk.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:34.743
It's one of my favorite things to do.

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:36.773
Cool? Yay.

